WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:24.188
There were three children: Gerald, Jimmy, and Kathleen.

2
00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:29.234
And they were at school in a little town in England.

3
00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:35.526
The boys were at one school, of course, and their sister was at another.

4
00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:39.122
They used to see each other only on weekends.

5
00:00:39.123 --> 00:00:45.100
So they looked forward to going home for summer vacation.

6
00:00:45.101 --> 00:00:50.577
But one year they couldn't go home because someone in the family had the measles.

7
00:00:50.578 --> 00:00:53.308
That disease was easy to catch.

8
00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:59.880
After many letters back and forth, their parents agreed to let them stay at Kathleen's school.

9
00:00:59.881 --> 00:01:02.038
All the girls had gone home.

10
00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:05.632
All the teachers had left except the French teacher.

11
00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:10.040
Now the boys had arrived, and they were drinking tea with Kathleen.

12
00:01:10.041 --> 00:01:13.722
"We need a summer project," she said.

13
00:01:13.723 --> 00:01:16.015
"Let's write a book."

14
00:01:16.016 --> 00:01:19.842
"Too much work," said Gerald, who was the oldest.

15
00:01:19.843 --> 00:01:21.629
"We'll do something outdoors.

16
00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.831
A cave would be good.

17
00:01:22.832 --> 00:01:24.910
We could eat our meals there."

18
00:01:24.911 --> 00:01:26.867
"There aren't any caves,"

19
00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:29.713
said Jimmy, who liked to say no.

20
00:01:29.714 --> 00:01:34.336
"And I doubt Mademoiselle will let us go out by ourselves."

21
00:01:34.337 --> 00:01:39.136
"Well, I'm going to talk to her," said Gerald.

22
00:01:39.137 --> 00:01:47.237
He washed his hands and combed his hair before he knocked on Mademoiselle's door.

23
00:01:47.238 --> 00:01:53.205
She was reading.

24
00:01:53.206 --> 00:01:57.001
"Excuse me, Mademoiselle," said Gerald politely.

25
00:01:57.002 --> 00:02:00.798
"I thought I'd say hello because you're in charge of us."

26
00:02:00.799 --> 00:02:04.585
Mademoiselle was charmed by the young man's manners.

27
00:02:04.586 --> 00:02:06.978
"Can I do anything for you?"

28
00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:08.208
"No, thank you.

29
00:02:08.209 --> 00:02:10.175
We don't want to be any trouble.

30
00:02:10.176 --> 00:02:15.766
In fact, we would cause less trouble tomorrow if we spent all day outside."

31
00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.881
Mademoiselle smiled.

32
00:02:17.882 --> 00:02:20.139
"I know what you really want.

33
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.707
You want to be left alone."

34
00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:26.253
Gerald laughed and Mademoiselle did too.

35
00:02:26.254 --> 00:02:28.817
"Go ahead," she said.

36
00:02:28.818 --> 00:02:32.182
"I won't stand in your way."

37
00:02:32.183 --> 00:02:36.094
The next morning the children went off on their adventure.

38
00:02:36.095 --> 00:02:38.564
It was a beautiful day.

39
00:02:38.565 --> 00:02:42.078
"We're sure to find something," said Gerald.

40
00:02:42.079 --> 00:02:45.157
"A boy at school said that there was a cave near here.

41
00:02:45.158 --> 00:02:47.738
But he said there's an enchanted castle too.

42
00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:50.662
So none of that may be true."

43
00:02:50.663 --> 00:02:54.649
The children walked along the road, which was very hot.

44
00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.871
They decided to share a drink from their lunch.

45
00:02:57.872 --> 00:03:00.797
Soon they came to a fork in the road.

46
00:03:00.798 --> 00:03:05.244
They went right and came to another fork and then another.

47
00:03:05.245 --> 00:03:15.374
"We're completely lost," said Kathleen. "What fun!"

48
00:03:15.375 --> 00:03:20.724
Now the trees arched overhead and bushes lined the banks along the road.

49
00:03:20.725 --> 00:03:23.822
"Let's have some lunch," said Jimmy.

50
00:03:23.823 --> 00:03:28.810
As they sat down, Gerald leaned against some bushes.

51
00:03:28.811 --> 00:03:31.917
"Oh my!" he cried.

52
00:03:31.918 --> 00:03:35.660
The bushes gave way and he almost fell backward.

53
00:03:35.661 --> 00:03:38.420
The other two pulled back the bushes.

54
00:03:38.421 --> 00:03:41.509
There was a large hole in the bank.

55
00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:46.038
"It's a cave!" said Gerald. "I'm going in."

56
00:03:46.039 --> 00:03:51.620
"Oh, don't!" said Kathleen. "There might be snakes."

57
00:03:51.621 --> 00:03:55.435
But Gerald was already crawling through the hole.

58
00:03:55.436 --> 00:03:58.571
"It is a cave! Come look!"

59
00:03:58.572 --> 00:04:01.962
Kathleen and Jimmy followed him down the hole.

60
00:04:01.963 --> 00:04:06.246
They walked a short distance and came out into the sunshine.

61
00:04:06.247 --> 00:04:10.256
"How wonderful!" said Kathleen.

62
00:04:10.257 --> 00:04:16.659
Ahead of them was a tall arch framed with ferns and grasses.

63
00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:20.612
"It looks like a train tunnel," said Jimmy.

64
00:04:20.613 --> 00:04:25.758
"It's the entrance to the enchanted castle," said Kathleen.

65
00:04:25.759 --> 00:04:27.366
"Oh, don't be silly."

66
00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.112
Gerald led the way to the arch.

67
00:04:30.113 --> 00:04:34.029
"There's a set of steps!" said Jimmy.

68
00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:39.064
They followed Gerald down the steps, walking slowly through the darkness.

69
00:04:39.065 --> 00:04:41.850
Up ahead was a patch of daylight.

70
00:04:41.851 --> 00:04:46.965
The children passed under another arch and out onto a terrace.

71
00:04:46.966 --> 00:04:50.154
Below them was a lake with an island.

72
00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:55.381
Beyond that, marble statues gleamed among the trees.

73
00:04:55.382 --> 00:04:58.764
White towers stood out against the sky.

74
00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:08.206
"It's the enchanted castle!" cried Kathleen.
